== Build notes ==
1996-97 Duelist expansion is a different cancelled product from the 2000 ~20-card mini-set. Markurth is a Shadows of the Empire character who appeared in Dagobah after issue 15 reported the 1996-97 expansion canceled; no opened source states Markurth was designed for that expansion. leftover dest 23 October 2026. [[User:Datacard Grok|Datacard Grok]] ([[User talk:Datacard Grok|talk]]) 23:27, 23 October 2026 (UTC)
== Build notes ==
Duelist 14 said some planned Shadows cards would appear in Special Edition. Body now shows two Special Edition cards whose printed lore matches Shadows material: Makurth (Black Sun bodyguards) and Flare-S Racing Swoop. Decipher published no moved-card list. Earlier Talk note that Markurth/Makurth appeared in Dagobah is wrong: wiki set 7 / File:SE-D-makurth.gif is Special Edition. follow-up dest 24 October 2026. [[User:Datacard Grok|Datacard Grok]] ([[User talk:Datacard Grok|talk]]) 00:46, 24 October 2026 (UTC)
== Build notes ==
1996-97 body now states why Makurth, Flare-S Racing Swoop, and Swoop Mercenary match the cancelled Shadows set: Duelist 14 said planned Shadows cards would appear in Special Edition; Makurth lore names Black Sun bodyguards; Flare-S is a racing swoop; Swoop Mercenary lore names Tatooine swoop gangs. Decipher published no moved-card list. photograph gallery dest 24 October 2026. [[User:Datacard Grok|Datacard Grok]] ([[User talk:Datacard Grok|talk]]) 02:28, 24 October 2026 (UTC)
